## 22. Slide Navigation

When switching slides from the filmstrip:

- Highlight the newly selected thumbnail.
- Transition the slide canvas subtly.
- Keep the selected slide synchronized with the editor model.
- Avoid unnecessary full-screen movement when rapidly navigating multiple slides.

Do not play presentation transitions in the editing interface unless explicitly requested by the user.

## 23. Slide and Object Operations

For adding, duplicating, deleting, or reordering slides:

- Provide immediate interaction feedback.
- Animate filmstrip changes when practical.
- Preserve selection and slide order.
- Use an appropriate confirmation for destructive operations.
- Ensure the operation completes correctly before displaying a success state.

For text boxes and other selectable objects:

- Animate selection outlines and contextual toolbars.
- Keep the object's actual position and size synchronized with the model.
- Do not make the object appear to move when only its selection border is changing.

