# PHASE 9 — PDF READER

## 24. Page Navigation and Zoom

For page changes:

- Use a subtle transition only when it improves orientation.
- Avoid a slow full-page fade for every small scroll.
- Keep continuous scrolling fluid.
- Maintain accurate page numbering.

For zoom:

- Preserve the user's focal point when zooming where feasible.
- Avoid animating the entire document independently of the user's pinch gesture.
- Keep annotation coordinates aligned with the PDF content.
- Avoid extra haptics during continuous pinch updates.

## 25. Annotation Tools

When switching between highlight, drawing, text-note, and selection modes:

- Animate the active tool state.
- Provide a subtle selection haptic when appropriate.
- Preserve the active annotation tool until the user changes it or the workflow requires exiting it.
- Do not trigger haptics on every pointer movement.
- Keep drawing responsive and accurate.

After an annotation is saved successfully, display an appropriate confirmation. If saving fails, preserve the annotation in memory where feasible and show a clear error.

